From 0bc50a898c334f8d3767dcb4a0c5339d6fa1d837 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 10:24:13 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] perf(worker): auto-size contiguous CUDA pool across shapes on
 64 KiB UMA

Pre-allocate a single contiguous caching-allocator scratch segment right
before model construction (after GPUModelRunner.__init__) on 64 KiB
integrated UMA CUDA hosts when native cudaMalloc caching is active and
>= 32 GiB of order-13 blocks are free. In direct_loader.bind_weight_arena,
once the rank's exact resident weight footprint is measured, keep the pool
when within <= 1 GiB (TP3 fast path) or evacuate any live tensors in the
scratch range, free the oversized scratch segment, soak MIGRATE_UNMOVABLE
sub-order-13 blocks, and allocate one exact-fit permanent weight pool
(scaled by draft_tensor_parallel_size when a speculator is configured).

This eliminates permanent boot-to-boot SMMU L3 page-table fragmentation
across every TP shape (TP1..TP8, with or without device Engram or
expert-slot offloading) and arbitrary model sizes while never pinning
unused host RAM or activating on 4 KiB kernels or discrete-VRAM GPUs.
Bypass _scoped_allocator_max_split(20) during load_model while anchored
and skip redundant buddy soaking in direct_loader.bind_weight_arena.

Upstream-base: 19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354
Quality: no numerical or algorithmic change; memory placement only.
Tests: pytest tests/v1/worker/test_contiguous_cuda_pool.py
       tests/model_executor/model_loader/test_direct_loader.py
       tests/model_executor/model_loader/test_direct_loader_cuda.py
       tests/v1/worker/test_engine_grid_sync.py (114 passed).
